    {
      "id": "tpl-col2",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 0.62,
      "y": 7.9,
      "w": 7.26,
      "z": 4,
      "md": "- **Two sets of rules.** Each year, ITEP applies 2026 law and Act 24 as enrolled to the same residents, with incomes held at 2026 levels.\n- **Average times residents.** The workbook shows −$812 per resident in 2031. Times about 766,000 residents (implied by the sheet), that is $622 million.\n- **Income tax, residents only.** Nonresidents and Act 24’s credit changes are left out. The Department of Taxation puts the whole act at about $300 million a year by 2031.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 13.5,
        "color": "#354F52",
        "leading": 1.4
      }
    },
